/// with an ordinary `to` must not leave the old answers reachable. The
/// tree-walker drops the entry when it runs the declaration; the bytecode
/// compiler emits this call for the same reason. Like [`LRU_CACHE_DECLARE`] it
/// carries a leading NUL, so no source identifier can name it.
pub const LRU_CACHE_CLEAR: &str = "\\u{0}lru_cache_clear";
